	</row>
	<row id="msg_0377_R30R0201_00030" index="30">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">A whole pile of strange coins!\fMaybe they’re from another country...</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0377_R30R0201_00031" index="31">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">MR. POKEMON: Visitors! And young\nones, with that first-week-on-\fthe-road shine. Sit, sit.\rI collect curiosities--and I’ve\nlearned that the smallest\fcuriosity often matters most.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0377_R30R0201_00032" index="32">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">MR. POKEMON: A held item is a\nlittle promise. Your Pokémon\fcarries it, and it may answer at\njust the right moment--not because\fyou were strong, but because you\nPREPARED.\rThis Quick Claw is not a shortcut.\nIt is a surprise. And surprises,\fin a tight spot, are sometimes\nenough.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0377_R30R0201_00033" index="33">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">MR. POKEMON: Go on. Clip it to one\nof yours.\rPreparation before power--that’s\nthe whole lesson, and most\fTrainers learn it far too late.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0377_R30R0201_00034" index="34">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">MR. POKEMON: Preparation before\npower! Most Trainers learn it far\ftoo late. You have a head start.</language>
	</row>
</body>
